DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the end of the semester with this brilliant showcase
  from our rising Visual Arts graduates! This exhibition marks the culmina
 tion of their degree\, launching their creative journeys. Each student pr
 esents a cohesive body of artwork in the Finley Galleries\, our final exh
 ibition of the Spring 2026 semester.\nMade to be Seen features an impress
 ive range of interdisciplinary approaches: mixed-media sculpture\, large-
 scale painting\, hand-sewn textiles\, ceramics\, video projection\, photo
 graphy\, and installations. Over 30 Visual Arts graduates invite you to e
 xplore their creative research and current perspectives\, on view through
  these vibrant capstone projects!  \n \nExhibiting Artists:Section 1: Ver
 onica Avignone\, Christian Campoverde\, Mae Elkovich\, Lisette Flor\, Emi
 ly Garces\, Aj Malabunga\, Jenna Mcdonough\, Melanie Medina\, Angeline Or
 tiz\, Tasir Plant\nSection 2: Mari Ahmed\, Chez Amos\, Kaila Craig\, Aman
 da Lerner\, Jeremiah Molin\, Kevin Pena\, Rose Perez Cruz\, Emmanuella Po
 nzio\, Daniel Portillo\, Liliana Salce\, Giacomo Valerin\, Beyza Yildiz\n
 Section 3: Duy-Minh Do\, Catalina Ferraro\, Keaoh Gonzalez\, Alexa Grasso
 \, Katelin Guaman\, Paulina Guerra\, Keita Mcfarlane\, Teiona Mcnair\, Lu
 z Plata\, Diana Valdes\, Lloyd Zheng\n \nMade to be SeenBA Visual Arts Th
 esis ExhibitionFinley Gallery\, Finley HallExhibition dates: April 23-29\
 , 2026Closing Reception: Wednesday April 29\, 6-8pm\n\nHosted by: Art and
  Design\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://montclair.camp
 uslabs.com/engage/event/12433034
