DESCRIPTION:"Rise Up" is a collaborative production presented by the Cente
 r for Latino heritage and Spanish language Excellence (CLaSE) and the Dep
 artment of Theater and Dance at Montclair State University\, in partnersh
 ip with the Montclair Fund for Educational Excellence (MFEE) and  Dr. Lis
 a Brenner\, Theatre & Dance Department at Drew University. \nThis showcas
 e features Latino students aged 12 to 17\, MSU students and members of ou
 r Kichwa community\,  primarily from Central and South America\, who have
  developed original works to express their feelings about their culture a
 nd the obstacles they have faced. The performance includes a diverse arra
 y of talents\, from monologues detailing personal histories in countries 
 like Honduras\, Mexico\, Guatemala\, etc.\, to choreographed dances and o
 riginal songs performed in both English and Spanish. \nThe "Rise Up" prod
 uction serves as a vital bridge between young Latino performers and the u
 niversity communities. By providing a professional stage for these studen
 ts to share their narratives of resilience and heritage during the Spring
  2026 season\, the project validates their artistic capabilities and rein
 forces their inner strength. This collaboration ensures that student voic
 es are not merely heard but celebrated\, fostering a deeper mutual unders
 tanding and a lasting connection within the community.\nCome to support t
 hese young talents and enjoy the show!\n\nHosted by: Center for Latino He
 ritage & Spanish Language Excellence\n\nAdditional Information can be fou
 nd at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12445276
